  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Latin American Dev. and Social Cohesion</narrative>
  </title>
  <description type="1">
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">The main objective of the project is to facilitate the creation of a locally-owned consensus on the post-crisis development agenda for Latin America, through a structured p  rocess of consultation and constructive debate that is grounded in the reality of individual countries.  There is urgency in finding a greater measure of agreement on practical development solutions for the 21st century which includes the goal of social cohesion.  The current crisis provides a clear opportunity: lessons and challenges are fresh in people&apos;s minds, and this makes it more likely that Latin American societies will respond positively to this initiative. Building of locally-owned consensus on the post-crisis development agenda for countries in Latin America, through a structured process of multi-stakeholder dialogues and constructive debate that is grounded in the reality and priorities of individual countries.</narrative>
  </description>
